      	<div type="translation" resp="part:emfr">
      		
      		<p n="1-2">Tirthy-second <supplied reason="subaudible">year</supplied> of the victorious king Ma<supplied reason="lost">yē</supplied>ntiraparumaṉ.<note>Sanskrit Mahendravarman.</note></p>
      		<p n="2-6"><supplied reason="subaudible">This is</supplied> the stone <supplied reason="subaudible">of</supplied> Akkantai Kōṭaṉ, the servant of Poṟmōtaṉṉār<note>Cf. Poṟmōtaṉār in DHARMA_INSPallava00281, same findspot, king, and year.<!--Update cros-ref--></note>, he who fell recapturing <supplied reason="explanation"><foreign>viṭuvittu</foreign><note>Literally "liberating".</note></supplied> cattle when <gap reason="ellipsis"/> <supplied reason="explanation"><foreign><!--<gap reason="lost" quantity="4" unit="character"/>--><!--Problem: <gap> not allowed within supplied-->yai</foreign></supplied> seized cattle.
      		</p>
      		
